From 64a32a67c8acbbae0126d9f2d05cc2ac95279994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:03:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ChopGimp 4.1.1: one object selection for every vector tool
 and panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- chopgimp_vobjects_style_targets(): the visible, unlocked leaves of the
  selection, the one list every style change edits (options bar, Aspect,
  colors, tool options); chopgimp_vobjects_style_undo(): one undo step per
  burst of the same change
- the fill / stroke options of the Pen, Shape, Curvature, Pencil… tools
  edit the selected objects, never the legacy view (object #1): a color
  chosen after drawing B no longer goes to A
- Direct Selection (A): the objects owning the selected nodes become the
  selection (rectangle, Shift+click adds an object, click in the void
  deselects); selected nodes survive a style change
- one watcher (chopgimp-tools.c): the foreground / background colors
  follow the selected object and recolor the selection with any vector
  tool; another active layer deselects the objects of the previous one;
  a vector layer added by the user has its objects selected
- Ctrl+A / Ctrl+Shift+A (and Ctrl+D) select all / no objects with a vector
  tool; the options bar shows « mixte » where the selected objects differ
